<p>Israeli forces intensified airstrikes across Lebanon on Sunday, hitting Beirut, towns east of the capital and areas in the south. The cited reports say the strikes killed dozens of people and wounded many more. One strike in Beirut&#x27;s Jnah neighborhood landed about 100 meters from Rafik Hariri University Hospital. Another, in Ain Saadeh, a predominantly Christian town many residents had long seen as safer than front-line areas, killed Lebanese Forces official Pierre Moawad, his wife Flavia and another woman. The escalation comes as Israel has widened its operations in Lebanon since early March, pairing airstrikes across the country with a ground offensive in the south after Hezbollah entered the regional war on the side of Iran, according to the provided reports. The latest attacks have deepened fears far beyond the border zone, put more pressure on already strained civilian infrastructure and sharpened concerns about Lebanon&#x27;s internal divisions as people displaced from the south seek refuge in places once seen as relatively insulated from the fighting.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/_J3SSk6yEz9L6xvCzV3VZfkFqRcV3luIuZNyD9nI_Zo3AnIvMC3xpNqDh5sHDRTgTaL_mMHG9Tptf35P4k4jLkG5l2niGJrx8UkcVHPq1ZB7' alt='Mutiple buildings hit by Israeli missiles in the Taybeh area of south Lebanon.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Child toll: Lebanese authorities say Israeli attacks on Lebanon since the start of the war have killed more than 1,400 people, including 126 children.</li><li>Warship claim: Hezbollah said it fired a cruise missile at an Israeli warship off the coast, while the Israeli military said it was &quot;not aware&quot; of any such incident.</li></ul><blockquote>Shortly after, the Israeli planes were flying overhead, and we - Nancy Hassan</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Lebanese Forces Party: The Christian political party publicly identified Pierre Moawad, a local party official, and his wife Flavia among those killed in Ain Saadeh, underscoring that the strike hit a constituency opposed to Hezbollah as well as Hezbollah-aligned areas. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1989319/israeli-strikes-leave-15-more-dead-in-lebanon'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Israeli military: After Hezbollah said it had launched a cruise missile at an Israeli warship, the Israeli military said it was &quot;not aware&quot; of any such incident. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1989319/israeli-strikes-leave-15-more-dead-in-lebanon'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Displaced Lebanese residents: Residents and people sheltering outside the usual conflict zones told Al Jazeera that the widening bombardment is aggravating social and sectarian tensions as communities debate who should bear the costs and risks of the war. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2026/4/7/creating-rift-part-of-game-plan-israeli-attacks-deepen-lebanon-fissures'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/06/world/middleeast/israel-attacks-lebanon-kill-dozens.html'>Israel Steps Up Attacks on Lebanon, Killing Dozens</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1989319/israeli-strikes-leave-15-more-dead-in-lebanon'>Israeli strikes leave 15 more dead in Lebanon</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2026/4/7/creating-rift-part-of-game-plan-israeli-attacks-deepen-lebanon-fissures'>‘They want to create a rift’: Israeli attacks deepen Lebanon fissures</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/05/middle-east-crisis-live-iran-israel-us-war-trump-strait-hormuz-missing-pilot-downed?CMP=share_btn_url&amp;page=with%3Ablock-69d2e99e8f080da25b48ba5c#block-69d2e99e8f080da25b48ba5c'>Christian anti-Hezbollah Lebanese Forces Party official Pierre Mouawad, his wife, and another woman are killed in an Israeli airstrike in Ain Saadeh, a predominantly Christian town east of Beirut, Lebanon. (The Guardian)</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>